Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the finance dashboard project.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a production dependency
- Used npm (the project's package manager) to install the package

### 2. Modified Files

#### finance-dashboard/package.json
- Added `@vercel/analytics: ^2.0.1` to the dependencies section

#### finance-dashboard/package-lock.json
- Updated lockfile with the new dependency and its 257 transitive dependencies
- Ensures consistent dependency resolution across environments

#### finance-dashboard/src/App.jsx
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main App component (inside the `<main>` element)
- Placed according to official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects

## Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Framework detected: React with Vite
- Analytics component added to the root App component to ensure tracking across all pages
- No additional configuration required for Vite-based React projects
- Component placement ensures proper analytics tracking for all user interactions

## Verification Steps Completed:

1. ✅ Build successful: `npm run build` completed without errors
2. ✅ Linter passed: `npm run lint` showed no errors or warnings
3. ✅ No tests to run: Project doesn't include test suite
4. ✅ Dependencies installed: package-lock.json properly updated

## Next Steps for User:

To enable analytics data collection on Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking is active by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
4. Analytics data will begin accumulating after deployment

## Technical Notes:

- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact page performance
- It automatically handles client-side page view tracking
- Works seamlessly with React's client-side routing
- No additional API keys or configuration needed when deployed to Vercel
